                                    "text": "param out_gain_db 0 @min -24 @max 12",
                                    "varname": "out_gain_db"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-43",
                                    "linecount": 60,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1178.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nvps_liquid_orbit — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nVector phaseshaping (VPS) applied to the tuba's own phase. The phaseshaper's\nbend point p = (d, v) sets the timbre: the centre (0.5, 0.5) is a pure sine\nin phase with the horn's fundamental, larger v grows a formant, and d far\nfrom 0.5 brightens it. The bend point orbits a Lissajous figure locked to the\nbar, so the bass \"talks\" and flows in time with the track.\n\nSource: Kleimola, Lazzarini, Timoney & Välimäki, DAFx-11 §3 (VPS), §3.1\n(formant crossfade), §4.3 (Lissajous modulation); Lazzarini, Timoney,\nPekonen & Välimäki, DAFx-09 (adaptive phase distortion).\n\nPARAMETERS (7 + output gain)\n\n1. d — 0.05…0.95, default 0.653\n   Horizontal bend point. 0.5 = symmetric; towards 0 or 1 = brighter, buzzier.\n\n2. v — 0.5…4, default 3.121\n   Vertical bend point. 0.5 = plain; 1 = pulse-like; 1.5–4 = a formant at\n   about (2v − 1) × f0, the vocal \"liquid\" peak.\n\n3. orbit — 0…100 %, default 100 %\n   Size of the Lissajous orbit around (d, v). 0 = static timbre.\n\n4. orbit_per_bar — 0.25…4, default 1\n   Orbit speed, snapped to 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2, 3 or 4 cycles per bar (always\n   in sync with the bar line, even across 4 bars).\n\n5. lissajous_ratio — 1…4 (stepped), default 2\n   How many times v moves for each turn of d. 1 = ellipse, 2 = figure-eight,\n   3–4 = knotted, more vowel changes per cycle.\n\n6. tone_hz — 200…12000 Hz, default 7000 Hz\n   Two-pole lowpass on the voice.\n\n7. wet — 0…100 %, default 100 %\n   Dry/wet crossfade. The voice is built on the horn's phase, so its\n   fundamental lines up with the dry note and the blend adds up in phase.\n\n8. out_gain_db — -24…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.\n- in3: f0 in Hz. 0 = disconnected -> fixed 55 Hz. No zero-crossing fallback.\n- in4: one-bar phasor. If held, an internal 2 s bar (120 BPM) takes over.\n- in5: phase-locked tuba phasor (the phase that is shaped). If static, an\n  internal ramp at f0 carries on from the last phase.\n- in6: pitch confidence. Low confidence fades the voice back to the plain\n  fundamental (no wild formants on unsure notes). If static, treated as 1.\n- out1 / out2: stereo (voice centred).\n\nNOTES\n- Non-integral formants use the paper's two-oscillator crossfade, so sweeping\n  v stays smooth instead of aliasing.\n- Gated by an internal envelope follower; silent when the horn is.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
