                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-33",
                                    "linecount": 55,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1081.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nssb_space_shift — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA single-sideband frequency shifter that moves every tuba partial by the same\nnumber of Hz — chosen as an exact 5-limit fraction of the horn's f0. That is\ndifferent from pitch shifting: the fundamental can stay put while the upper\npartials land between the harmonic series, which is the bell-like, hollow,\n\"space bass\" colour. Feedback re-shifts the shifted signal, so partials climb\n(or fall) in a barber-pole spiral.\n\nSource: Wardle, DAFx-98 (Hilbert-transformer frequency shifter); Esqueda,\nVälimäki & Parker, DAFx-15 paper 67 (SSB / barber-pole shifting).\n\nPARAMETERS (5 + output gain)\n\n1. interval — 0…4 (stepped), default 0\n   0 = f0/4, 1 = f0/3, 2 = f0/2, 3 = 2f0/3, 4 = 3f0/4. The shift is the\n   interval × f0 in Hz, all 5-limit; the horn keeps its pitch centre while the\n   spectrum goes inharmonic. f0/2 is the classic \"half-speed ghost\" setting.\n\n2. direction — 0 = down, 1 = up, default 1\n   Which sideband survives. Up glides the partials upward (rising, airy); down\n   pulls them under the fundamental (dark, subby, unsettling).\n\n3. glide — 0…1, default 0.0\n   Smoothing of the shift frequency, 3 ms to 500 ms. Short tracks every tuba\n   note exactly; long makes the shift slide between notes like a tape stop.\n\n4. feedback — 0…0.7, default 0.555\n   Regeneration around the shifter. 0 is a single clean shift; 0.3–0.5 makes\n   metallic barber-pole sidebands that grow as the note sustains. The loop is\n   tanh-limited, so it will not run away.\n\n5. mix — 0…1, default 1.0\n   Dry tuba against the shifted signal. 0.5–0.7 keeps the horn recognisable\n   while the inharmonic layer sits around it.\n\n6. out_gain_db — -24…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.\n- in3: f0 in Hz. 0 or out-of-range means \"unknown\": the last valid pitch is\n  held (init 55 Hz). No zero-crossing fallback.\n- in4: bound only — the shift is a fixed interval, not a bar-synced motion.\n- out1 / out2: stereo.\n\nNOTES\n- Quadrature is the four-section one-pole allpass pair (the same coefficients\n  used by the repo's Hilbert effects); the shift is exact for 44.1–48 kHz.\n- A 12 Hz DC blocker after the shifter removes the offset produced when a\n  partial lands at 0 Hz.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
