                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-42",
                                    "linecount": 58,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1139.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nsideband_sub_growl — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nFM of the whole horn with the sidebands split four ways: below or above each\nnote, odd or even. Keep mostly the lower ones and the horn grows a growling\nsub-harmonic undertone; swing toward the upper ones and it screeches. The bar\nmorphs between the two, and the FM index opens as you play louder.\n\nSource: Lazzarini, Timoney & Lysaght, DAFx-08 paper 42 §3.1–3.2\neq. 5–20 (adaptive split-sideband synthesis), §4.3 (lower-sideband\nsub-harmonics, upper-sideband screech).\nParents: 15_inst_split_sideband_morph_synth, 07_adaptive_split_sideband.\n\nPARAMETERS (7 + output gain)\n\n1. cm_ratio — 0.5…4, default 2\n   Modulator = f0 / cm_ratio. 2 = sidebands every half-harmonic (lower\n   ones = sub-octave growl); 3 = thirds; 1 = harmonic.\n\n2. index — 0…6, default 2\n   FM index (scaled 40–100 % by the envelope). 0 = clean.\n\n3. low_high — -100…+100 %, default 100 %\n   - = keep lower sidebands (sub, dark), + = keep upper (bright, screech),\n   0 = both (plain FM).\n\n4. odd_even — -100…+100 %, default -100 %\n   - = odd sidebands only (hollow), + = even only (octave-y, smooth).\n\n5. bar_morph — 0…100 %, default 0 %\n   Bar swing of low_high (sine, ± this amount).\n\n6. morph_div — 1…16 (stepped), default 2\n   Morphs per bar.\n\n7. blend — 0…100 %, default 80 %\n   Dry/wet. The dry comes from the same Hilbert network, so they never comb.\n\n8. out_gain_db — -24…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.\n- in3: f0 in Hz. 0 = disconnected -> fixed 55 Hz. No zero-crossing fallback.\n- in4: one-bar phasor (morph). If held, an internal 2 s bar (120 BPM) runs.\n- in5: smoothed tuba envelope (index). If static, an internal follower is\n  used.\n- out1 / out2: stereo.\n\nNOTES\n- Sidebands are computed exactly from Bessel J0–J10 (no Hilbert on the\n  modulator), so the split is clean; the horn side uses the 4-stage\n  Hilbert pair (best below ~1 kHz).\n- Level is auto-compensated for removed sidebands (exact for a sine\n  carrier). A 10 Hz DC blocker removes sidebands that fold onto 0 Hz.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
